// ROTATION IS A REFUSING STEP, NOT A RECORDED INTENTION (machine-intake design
// doc §6 and its discriminating control in §16: "Leave factory credential
// working after rotation | BmcSecure refuses"). The phase's required result is
// stated there as a CONJUNCTION over two independent readbacks — the unique
// managed credential works AND the published factory credential no longer
// works — and the second half is the one every ordinary rotation script drops:
// creating an account and getting a 201 back says nothing about whether the
// bootstrap login still opens a session. A phase that recorded only the first
// half would report BmcSecure satisfied on a machine that any reader of the
// vendor's published default can still log into, which is the
// fabricated-plausible-output failure of DESIGN §5 aimed at the one phase whose
// whole purpose is to close that door.
//
// This module owns the WORKFLOW STANDING of that conjunction. It observes
// nothing: extdeps.bmc owns the external shapes, the effectful rotation
// actuator owns the observation, and the fold below owns what a set of
// readbacks may and may not conclude. Its route to a consumer is
// bmc_secure_phase_receipt, whose envelope is read by
// gunbc.machine_intake_disposition.derive_fleet_admission exactly as every
// other phase's is; there is no second admission path for credentials.
//
// WHY THE VOCABULARY IS NOT gunbc.bmc_onboarding's. That module is quarantined
// legacy (machine-intake ruling 2026-08-29, answer (b)): its
// FactoryDefault -> CredentialsRotated progression ADVANCES ITSELF with pure
// functions and consumes no readback at all, so it cannot refuse. This is the
// BMC-security extraction the ruling's §14 names, and it imports nothing from
// that module by construction — the quarantine witness requires exactly that
// no name bridges the two.

// WHAT ONE AUTHENTICATION ATTEMPT ESTABLISHED. Three arms, and the third is
// not the second wearing a softer name: a probe that could not run proves
// nothing about whether the credential works. Reading Unestablished as
// Rejected is the absorbing fallback of DESIGN §5 applied to the exact place
// it does the most damage — an unreachable account service would silently
// certify that the published credential had been retired.
type CredentialProbeOutcome
  = CredentialAccepted { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | CredentialRejected { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn credential_probe_evidence(outcome: CredentialProbeOutcome) -> EvidenceRef? {
  match outcome {
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => Present { value: e }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => Present { value: e }
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: _ } => none
  }
}

// THE RECEIPT NEVER CONTAINS THE PASSWORD, AND HAS NOWHERE TO PUT ONE (design
// §6). This is the durable half of a rotation: WHERE the credential lives and
// WHICH generation it is. There is no Secret-typed field on this record or on
// anything reachable from it, so redaction is unnecessary — the excluded state
// has no constructor (DESIGN §4b rung 4) rather than a validator that strips it.
//
// The location is a SecretRef because gunbc.secret_provision already owns where
// this fleet's secrets live (fleet_secret_ref); a fresh `secret_name: NonEmptyStr`
// beside it — which is what gunbc.bmc_onboarding's plan carries — is the second
// name for one concept DESIGN §3 forbids.
type ManagedCredentialReference {
  account: NonEmptyStr
  role: RedfishAccountRole
  secret: SecretRef
  credential_epoch: Int
}

// WHETHER THE ROTATION WAS APPLIED AT ALL, and when. applied_at is on the
// APPLICATION rather than beside it because the two readbacks below are only
// evidence about the rotation if they were taken after it; a rotation with no
// time has no ordering to check against, and the ordering is what stops a
// pre-rotation "the published credential was already rejected" reading from
// being replayed as the post-rotation proof.
//
// WHAT THE ORDERING DOES NOT ESTABLISH, said here so it is not read off the
// refusal names: these are times carried on SUPPLIED observations, so the fold
// enforces an ordering AMONG THE READINGS IT WAS HANDED and establishes nothing
// about whether any BMC was probed at all. That is the boundary DESIGN §4b
// keeps off the ladder — an external fact, observed at a declared frontier and
// never fabricated here. The frontier is the effectful rotation actuator that
// produces BmcCredentialRotationObservation; it does not exist yet, and it is
// the same producer the machine-intake ruling gates on the gunbc.bmc_onboarding
// split.
type CredentialRotationApplication
  = RotationApplied { reference: ManagedCredentialReference, applied_at: EpochMs, evidence: EvidenceRef }
  | RotationNotAttempted
  | AccountManagementUnavailable { detail: NonEmptyStr }

// ONE LAN PROBE, ADDRESSED TO ONE CENSUS MEMBER. The join matches when BOTH
// channel and assigned IPv4 agree (DESIGN §5: completeness is an identity
// join, not a count, and not a disjunction). A probe that names the member's
// channel and a different address, or the member's address and a different
// channel, covers no member: a rejection observed at 9.9.9.9 cannot close
// 10.0.0.1. The old single published_probe minted BmcSecured while a second
// LAN address still accepted; a disjunctive key would reopen that arm.
type PublishedCredentialLanProbe {
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber
  address: Ipv4Address
  outcome: CredentialProbeOutcome
}

// HOW THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT WOULD RETURN. Firmware reset is the MegaRAC
// residual measured on Mt. Collins unit 1: the disabled factory user remains
// on the controller and a firmware reset restores it. Administrator re-enable
// is the other documented restore, not a prose note.
type PublishedCredentialRestorePath
  = FirmwareResetRestoresPublishedAccount
  | AdministratorReEnableRestoresPublishedAccount

// A DELIBERATE BACKDOOR IS A NAMED POLICY OUTCOME, NEVER AN OPEN MACHINE.
// Break-glass is the default: a credential we own (SecretRef, never a
// password, never the published factory login). Keeping the published
// factory password is a separately named choice because that password is
// public and grants power, console, virtual media and firmware flash to
// anyone on the BMC network.
type RetainedCredentialKind
  = BreakGlassAccount { secret: SecretRef }
  | PublishedFactoryCredential

// THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT'S STANDING ON THE CONTROLLER, independent of whether
// a LAN probe rejected. Rejected-on-LAN and deleted-from-the-user-list are
// different facts: a disabled user still exists, and BmcSecured must say so.
// observed_at is ordered against rotation applied_at in adjudicate_published_census
// (PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation); a pre-rotation user-list cannot
// label the post-rotation standing.
// RetainedByPolicy is a third arm: it satisfies the BMC-secure conjunct
// ONLY under DevelopmentAndTest. Production refuses it; that refusal is the
// discriminating control for the day a machine is promoted.
type PublishedCredentialAccountObservation
  = PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired {
      restore_path: PublishedCredentialRestorePath
      evidence: EvidenceRef
      observed_at: EpochMs
    }
  | PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy {
      retention: RetainedCredentialKind
      evidence: EvidenceRef
      observed_at: EpochMs
    }

// THE OBSERVATION, BOUND TO ITS SUBJECT AND ITS CONTROLLER. sole_constructor
// keeps a caller from spelling the record beside the mint; it does not make the
// caller honest about where the readbacks came from, and this module does not
// claim it does. What it does hold is that the readings are carried together with
// the attempt they were taken for, so a rotation observed on one unit can never
// be presented as another's — the same join gunbc.machine_intake_access
// performs before the delivery solver runs.
//
// previous_credential_epoch is the epoch this unit stood at BEFORE the attempt:
// a rotation that re-writes the same generation is not a rotation.
//
// THE SINGLE published_probe FIELD IS GONE. It answered "did this one host
// reject" and minted BmcSecured while a second LAN address on the same
// controller still accepted. The published-credential readback is now a census
// of every channel the controller reported, plus a probe list joined to that
// census by identity. An empty census is not a one-host observation wearing a
// new name: it refuses rather than adjudicate.
type BmcCredentialRotationObservation sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  previous_credential_epoch: Int
  bootstrap_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome
  rotation: CredentialRotationApplication
  managed_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef
  census_observed_at: EpochMs
  published_probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>
  published_user: IpmiUserId
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation
}

fn observed_bmc_credential_rotation(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  previous_credential_epoch: Int,
  bootstrap_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  rotation: CredentialRotationApplication,
  managed_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  published_probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
) -> BmcCredentialRotationObservation {
  BmcCredentialRotationObservation {
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    previous_credential_epoch: previous_credential_epoch,
    bootstrap_probe: bootstrap_probe,
    rotation: rotation,
    managed_probe: managed_probe,
    channel_census: channel_census,
    census_evidence: census_evidence,
    census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
    published_probes: published_probes,
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: published_account,
  }
}

// EVERY WAY THE STEP REFUSES, each naming which reading failed rather than a
// generic "rotation failed". Two of the three access states the design doc
// names keep their names from that ruling: CredentialStateUnknown and
// PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired. The third is renamed here to
// AccountManagementUnreachable, because AccountManagementUnavailable is already
// the arm of CredentialRotationApplication that says the service did not
// answer, and one spelling for the OBSERVATION and the REFUSAL derived from it
// would be one name for two facts — a fork of exactly the kind DESIGN §3 names,
// inside a single module.
//
// PublishedCredentialStillAccepted is the discriminating refusal this phase
// exists for: everything else about the rotation succeeded and the machine is
// still open on its published default.
type BmcSecureRefusalCause
  = RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: MachineIntakeSubject, found: MachineIntakeSubject }
  | CredentialStateUnknown { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired
  | AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | CredentialRotationNotApplied
  | CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: Int, observed: Int }
  | ManagedCredentialRejected
  | ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, probed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, probed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken
  | PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember
  | PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedForProduction
  | PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }

// NO ARM RETURNS UnitHardware, AND THAT IS THE POINT (design §6: a non-working
// factory credential is an access state -> PartsHold, not ReturnWindow, absent
// other evidence). gunbc.machine_intake_disposition routes a UnitHardware
// refusal to ReturnWindow, which starts a return clock against the seller; a
// credential the operator has not rotated, an unreachable account service and a
// readback we could not take are not defects of the unit. Because the receipt's
// owner is derived here rather than authored at the call site, no caller can
// file a rotation refusal as a hardware defect.
fn bmc_secure_refusal_owner(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> QualificationRefusalOwner {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => BmcAccess
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => OperatorAction
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => OperatorAction
    ManagedCredentialRejected => OperatorAction
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedForProduction => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => "rotation observation belongs to another intake attempt"
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => "bootstrap credential probe did not establish a credential state"
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => "bootstrap credential no longer authenticates; the previously rotated credential is required"
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => "bmc account management was unreachable"
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => "no credential rotation was applied"
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => "credential epoch did not advance past the epoch this unit already stood at"
    ManagedCredentialRejected => "the rotated managed credential does not authenticate"
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the rotated managed credential readback did not establish a credential state"
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => "the managed credential readback precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => "the published factory credential still authenticates after rotation on a census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the published factory credential readback did not establish whether it still authenticates"
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => "the published credential readback precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => "the channel census was taken before the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => "the published-account user-list reading precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => "no controller channel census was taken; a single-address probe cannot adjudicate retirement"
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => "the channel census contained no addressable LAN member to probe"
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => "a LAN census member has no usable address and the published account still has access on that channel"
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => "the published account still has channel access (not NO ACCESS) on a census member"
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => "Get User Access for the published user was not present on a census member"
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => "more than one Get User Access row matched the published user on the same census member"
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => "a census LAN member has no matching published-credential probe"
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => "more than one published-credential probe matched the same census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => "a published-credential probe matched no census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedForProduction => "a retained BMC backdoor is not admitted for production; a fresh census pass that retires or disables the published credential is required"
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => "the declared factory-credential retention was not observed on a census LAN member"
  }
}

// The satisfied terminal keeps the reference and the readings it rests on, so a
// later reader can say WHICH rotation secured the unit and WHERE its evidence
// is. The password is not among them, structurally.
//
// published_credential SITS ON BmcSecured, NOT AS A REFUSAL AND NOT AS A
// SECOND SATISFIED COPRODUCT ARM. DisabledNotRetired is a real secured
// outcome: every addressable LAN member rejected the published credential, so
// the phase conjunction holds now. The residual is that a typed restore path
// would bring the account back. A third BmcSecureOutcome arm that also mapped
// to ReceiptSatisfied would be two names for one satisfied standing. A refusal
// would file a currently-closed published login as an unsatisfied phase and
// block fleet admission for a residual that is not an open session. The
// residual travels with the standing; it does not reopen the door.
// latest_admitted_probe_at is the max observed_at among admitted LAN probes,
// including accepted probes on the factory-retention path — not census
// order, and not a claim about when the door closed.
type BmcSecureOutcome
  = BmcSecured {
      endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
      reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
      evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
      latest_admitted_probe_at: EpochMs,
      published_credential: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
    }
  | BmcSecureRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }

// THE STANDING CARRIES THE SUBJECT AND THE QUALIFICATION POLICY IT WAS
// ADJUDICATED UNDER, AND BOTH JOINS ARE SEALED. An earlier cut returned the
// outcome alone and had bmc_secure_phase_receipt take the subject as a
// separate argument, so a standing legitimately derived for host A could be
// handed to the receipt function beside host B's subject. The same hatch
// existed for policy: derive wrote DevelopmentAndTest and the receipt took a
// second Production policy, restamping the digest. The receipt now reads
// subject and policy off the standing; there is no parameter left to swap.
// Promotion is a fresh derive_bmc_secure under Production, which refuses
// RetainedByPolicy. There is no observed environment on the unit; the policy
// is the declared qualification (FleetAdmissionReceipt already binds its
// digest). A caller can still declare DevelopmentAndTest — that is the policy
// fact, not a second knob beside the receipt.
//
// So the subject and the outcome are ONE record and the record is
// sole_constructor: derive_bmc_secure is its only mint, and the receipt
// projection reads the subject off the standing rather than accepting one. A
// cross-attempt replay has no argument left to swap.
//
// THE CEILING, SCOPED RATHER THAN OVERCLAIMED, on this repository's own
// precedent (gunbc.auth.secret_access_admission, and the coproduct-variant form
// falsified at test.claim.inventory_admitted_ledger_seal_livetree_witness_test):
// sole_constructor seals RECORDS, not coproduct arms, which is why the pairing
// and not the outcome is the sealed carrier — a caller may still write a
// BmcSecured OUTCOME literal, and it reaches nothing, because every consumer
// takes the standing. And the seal is not claimed for the emitted-Rust path,
// where DESIGN records by execution that a sole_constructor type's emitted
// mirror is forgeable; that is a known gap in the mechanism, not a property of
// this carrier.
//
// The seal was taken as a fixture-boundary red once during authoring -- a
// foreign module writing the record literal refuses with
// "sole_constructor type 'BmcSecureStanding' cannot be constructed outside its
// defining module" -- and is not re-enrolled here as a standing gate, because
// the mechanism's general coverage is gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus
// sole_constructor_cross_module_class and its probes; a per-carrier copy of
// that gate would be the redundant work DESIGN §2 prices. The witness obtains
// every standing FROM derive_bmc_secure, cross-module, so what is confined is
// the construction and not the type's usability.
type BmcSecureStanding sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  policy: IntakeQualificationPolicy
  outcome: BmcSecureOutcome
}

fn bmc_secure_evidence(
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  managed: EvidenceRef,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  published_probe_evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
  account_evidence: EvidenceRef,
) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  let head = match credential_probe_evidence(outcome: bootstrap) {
    Present { value: e } => [e]
    Absent => []
  }
  concat(concat(concat(head, [rotation_evidence, managed, census_evidence]), published_probe_evidence), [account_evidence])
}

fn published_account_evidence(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> EvidenceRef {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
  }
}

fn published_account_observed_at(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> EpochMs {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
  }
}

fn published_account_requires_published_closed(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> Bool {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => true
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => true
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: k, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match k {
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: _ } => true
        PublishedFactoryCredential => false
      }
  }
}

// Join identity is (channel, address). Packed as one Int so the census fold looks up
// rather than scanning probes per member (DESIGN §6: a quadratic fold is always fixed).
fn published_lan_identity_key(channel: IpmiChannelNumber, address: Ipv4Address) -> Int {
  ((channel as Int) * 4294967296)
    + ((((address.octet1 as Int) * 16777216) + ((address.octet2 as Int) * 65536))
      + ((address.octet3 as Int) * 256) + (address.octet4 as Int))
}

type PublishedProbeSlot
  = OneProbe { probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe }
  | SeveralProbes

fn insert_published_probe_slot(
  acc: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  p: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
) -> Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot> {
  let key = published_lan_identity_key(channel: p.channel, address: p.address)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, OneProbe { probe: p })
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        OneProbe { probe: _ } => map_insert(acc, key, SeveralProbes)
        SeveralProbes => acc
      }
  }
}

fn index_published_probes(probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>) -> Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot> {
  fold(probes, init: empty_map(), f: (acc, p) => insert_published_probe_slot(acc: acc, p: p))
}

fn bump_assigned_lan_identity(
  acc: Map<Int, Int>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
) -> Map<Int, Int> {
  let key = published_lan_identity_key(channel: channel, address: address)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, 1)
    Present { value: n } => map_insert(acc, key, n + 1)
  }
}

fn index_assigned_lan_identities(members: List<IpmiChannelCensusMember>) -> Map<Int, Int> {
  fold(
    members,
    init: empty_map(),
    f: (acc, m) =>
      match m {
        IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: _, medium: _ } => acc
        IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
          match cfg {
            IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned => acc
            IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } => bump_assigned_lan_identity(acc: acc, channel: ch, address: a)
          }
      },
  )
}

type CensusJoinProgress
  = CensusJoinOpen { evidence: List<EvidenceRef>, latest_admitted_probe_at: EpochMs?, saw_addressable_lan: Bool }
  | CensusJoinClosed { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }

// ONE SOURCE for whether an assigned-LAN probe admits or refuses. A later
// re-match of probe.outcome that closed Accepted/Unestablished independently
// made the RED-1 mutation receipt void (review 65033): changing this function's
// Accepted arm to none still closed in the caller with the same cause.
type PublishedProbeAdjudication
  = PublishedProbeRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }

fn adjudicate_published_probe(
  probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> PublishedProbeAdjudication {
  match probe.outcome {
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } =>
      PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: d } }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: e, observed_at: at } =>
      if require_published_closed {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: channel } }
      } else if at < applied_at {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
      } else {
        PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: e, observed_at: at }
      }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: e, observed_at: at } =>
      if require_published_closed {
        if at < applied_at {
          PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
        } else {
          PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: e, observed_at: at }
        }
      } else {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: channel } }
      }
  }
}

type LaterAdmittedProbeTime
  = TakePrevious
  | TakeObserved

fn later_admitted_probe_time_choice(prev_i: Int, observed_i: Int) -> LaterAdmittedProbeTime {
  if prev_i < observed_i {
    TakeObserved
  } else {
    TakePrevious
  }
}

fn later_admitted_probe_at(previous: EpochMs?, observed_at: EpochMs) -> EpochMs {
  match previous {
    Absent => observed_at
    Present { value: prev } =>
      match later_admitted_probe_time_choice(prev_i: prev as Int, observed_i: observed_at as Int) {
        TakePrevious => prev
        TakeObserved => observed_at
      }
  }
}

fn join_open_assigned_lan(
  ev: List<EvidenceRef>,
  previous: EpochMs?,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match map_get(probe_index, published_lan_identity_key(channel: channel, address: address)) {
    Absent => CensusJoinClosed { cause: PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralProbes => CensusJoinClosed { cause: PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneProbe { probe: probe } =>
          match adjudicate_published_probe(probe: probe, channel: channel, applied_at: applied_at, require_published_closed: require_published_closed) {
            PublishedProbeRefused { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
            PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: pe, observed_at: at } =>
              CensusJoinOpen {
                evidence: concat(ev, [pe]),
                latest_admitted_probe_at: Present { value: later_admitted_probe_at(previous: previous, observed_at: at) },
                saw_addressable_lan: true,
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn join_assigned_lan_member(
  progress: CensusJoinProgress,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match progress {
    CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
    CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: _ } =>
      join_open_assigned_lan(
        ev: ev,
        previous: latest,
        channel: channel,
        address: address,
        probe_index: probe_index,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        require_published_closed: require_published_closed,
      )
  }
}

fn published_user_access_key(channel: IpmiChannelNumber, user: IpmiUserId) -> Int {
  ((channel as Int) * 64) + (user as Int)
}

type PublishedUserAccessSlot
  = OneUserAccess { access: IpmiUserChannelAccess }
  | SeveralUserAccess

fn insert_published_user_access_slot(
  acc: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  row: IpmiUserChannelAccess,
) -> Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot> {
  let key = published_user_access_key(channel: row.channel, user: row.user)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, OneUserAccess { access: row })
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        OneUserAccess { access: _ } => map_insert(acc, key, SeveralUserAccess)
        SeveralUserAccess => acc
      }
  }
}

fn index_published_user_access(rows: List<IpmiUserChannelAccess>) -> Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot> {
  fold(rows, init: empty_map(), f: (acc, row) => insert_published_user_access_slot(acc: acc, row: row))
}

fn published_user_privilege_on_channel(
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(access_index, published_user_access_key(channel: channel, user: published_user)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralUserAccess => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneUserAccess { access: row } =>
          if row.privilege == IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess {
            none
          } else {
            Present { value: PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: channel } }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn unaddressed_lan_published_access_cause(
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(access_index, published_user_access_key(channel: channel, user: published_user)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralUserAccess => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneUserAccess { access: row } =>
          if row.privilege == IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess {
            none
          } else {
            Present { value: PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: channel } }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn join_census_member(
  progress: CensusJoinProgress,
  member: IpmiChannelCensusMember,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match progress {
    CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
    CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw } =>
      match member {
        IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _ } =>
          match published_user_privilege_on_channel(access_index: access_index, channel: ch, published_user: published_user) {
            Present { value: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
            Absent => CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw }
          }
        IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
          match cfg {
            IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned =>
              match unaddressed_lan_published_access_cause(access_index: access_index, channel: ch, published_user: published_user) {
                Present { value: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
                Absent => CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw }
              }
            IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } =>
              join_assigned_lan_member(
                progress: CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: true },
                channel: ch,
                address: a,
                probe_index: probe_index,
                applied_at: applied_at,
                require_published_closed: require_published_closed,
              )
          }
      }
  }
}

fn probe_unmatched_or_duplicate(
  probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
  assigned_index: Map<Int, Int>,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(assigned_index, published_lan_identity_key(channel: probe.channel, address: probe.address)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: probe.channel } }
    Present { value: n } =>
      if n > 1 {
        Present { value: PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: probe.channel } }
      } else {
        none
      }
  }
}

fn unmatched_published_probe_cause(
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  assigned_index: Map<Int, Int>,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  fold(
    probes,
    init: none,
    f: (acc, p) =>
      match acc {
        Present { value: c } => Present { value: c }
        Absent => probe_unmatched_or_duplicate(probe: p, assigned_index: assigned_index)
      },
  )
}

// THE PUBLISHED-CREDENTIAL READBACK IS A FOLD OVER THE CONTROLLER CHANNEL
// CENSUS. Assigned LAN members still require an identity-joined login probe.
// Unaddressed LAN (0.0.0.0) and non-LAN members join on Get User Access for
// observation.published_user: NO ACCESS closes the member; any other privilege
// refuses; a missing or duplicated (channel, user) row refuses. A NO ACCESS
// row for a different user does not close this one (review 65645).
// That is the unit-1 fact: channel 7 is 802.3 with a permanent unspecified
// address, and the rotation set admin to NO ACCESS on ch2, ch7 and ch8.
// Treating unaddressed as unconditionally open would refuse that controller
// forever (DESIGN §4d over-prohibition). An unaddressed channel that still
// holds ADMINISTRATOR is the exposure the moment it gets an address.
// A census taken before rotation is not the universe that join is complete
// against: a channel the rotation enabled would be absent from the roster.
// adjudicate_published_census_join refuses CensusPrecedesRotation once, before
// the fold, so assigned-LAN members cannot skip the ordering the unaddressed
// and non-LAN arms used to carry twice.
//
// RUNG: mechanically preventable. Ceiling is enrolled one-arm mutants on the
// merge path (DESIGN §4b(4)): a deletion of a guarding arm that reddens exactly
// the named witness. Next-rung trigger: that mutation capability for
// test.claim.machine_intake_bmc_secure_witness_test on required CI, not a
// scratch-tree one-shot. Named-cause witnesses in that module are the enrolled
// evidence this PR keeps executing. Do not cite an un-enrolled local run.
fn adjudicate_published_census_join(
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  managed_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  if list_length(items: census.members) == 0 {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken }
  } else if census_observed_at < applied_at {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, observed_at: census_observed_at },
    }
  } else {
    let require_closed = published_account_requires_published_closed(account: published_account)
    let probe_index = index_published_probes(probes: probes)
    let assigned_index = index_assigned_lan_identities(members: census.members)
    let access_index = index_published_user_access(rows: census.user_access)
    let joined = fold(
      census.members,
      init: CensusJoinOpen { evidence: [], latest_admitted_probe_at: none, saw_addressable_lan: false },
      f: (acc, m) => join_census_member(
        progress: acc,
        member: m,
        probe_index: probe_index,
        access_index: access_index,
        published_user: published_user,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        require_published_closed: require_closed,
      ),
    )
    match joined {
      CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: c }
      CensusJoinOpen { evidence: pev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw } =>
        if saw == false {
          BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember }
        } else {
          match unmatched_published_probe_cause(probes: probes, assigned_index: assigned_index) {
            Present { value: c } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: c }
            Absent =>
              match latest {
                Absent => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember }
                Present { value: at } =>
                  BmcSecured {
                    endpoint: endpoint,
                    reference: reference,
                    evidence: bmc_secure_evidence(
                      bootstrap: bootstrap,
                      rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
                      managed: managed_evidence,
                      census_evidence: census_evidence,
                      published_probe_evidence: pev,
                      account_evidence: published_account_evidence(account: published_account),
                    ),
                    latest_admitted_probe_at: at,
                    published_credential: published_account,
                  }
              }
          }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn adjudicate_published_census(
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  managed_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
  environment: MachineOperatingEnvironment,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  let account_at = published_account_observed_at(account: published_account)
  if account_at < applied_at {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, observed_at: account_at },
    }
  } else {
    match published_account {
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match environment {
        Production => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedForProduction }
        DevelopmentAndTest =>
          adjudicate_published_census_join(
            endpoint: endpoint,
            reference: reference,
            applied_at: applied_at,
            rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
            bootstrap: bootstrap,
            managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
            census: census,
            census_evidence: census_evidence,
            census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
            probes: probes,
            published_user: published_user,
            published_account: published_account,
          )
      }
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      adjudicate_published_census_join(
        endpoint: endpoint,
        reference: reference,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
        bootstrap: bootstrap,
        managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
        census: census,
        census_evidence: census_evidence,
        census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
        probes: probes,
        published_user: published_user,
        published_account: published_account,
      )
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      adjudicate_published_census_join(
        endpoint: endpoint,
        reference: reference,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
        bootstrap: bootstrap,
        managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
        census: census,
        census_evidence: census_evidence,
        census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
        probes: probes,
        published_user: published_user,
        published_account: published_account,
      )
  }
  }
}

// The managed credential must work, and must have been read after the rotation
// that created it. A pre-rotation acceptance would be a reading of whatever
// account already answered to that name.
fn adjudicate_managed_probe(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  managed: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  environment: MachineOperatingEnvironment,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  match managed {
    CredentialRejected { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialRejected }
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: me, observed_at: at } =>
      if at < applied_at {
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
      } else {
        adjudicate_published_census(
          endpoint: observation.endpoint,
          reference: reference,
          applied_at: applied_at,
          rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
          bootstrap: observation.bootstrap_probe,
          managed_evidence: me,
          census: observation.channel_census,
          census_evidence: observation.census_evidence,
          census_observed_at: observation.census_observed_at,
          probes: observation.published_probes,
          published_user: observation.published_user,
          published_account: observation.published_account,
          environment: environment,
        )
      }
  }
}

fn adjudicate_rotation(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  environment: MachineOperatingEnvironment,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  if (reference.credential_epoch <= observation.previous_credential_epoch) {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: CredentialEpochNotAdvanced {
        previous: observation.previous_credential_epoch,
        observed: reference.credential_epoch,
      },
    }
  } else {
    adjudicate_managed_probe(
      observation: observation,
      reference: reference,
      applied_at: applied_at,
      rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
      managed: observation.managed_probe,
      environment: environment,
    )
  }
}

fn adjudicate_bootstrap(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  environment: MachineOperatingEnvironment,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  match observation.bootstrap_probe {
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: CredentialStateUnknown { detail: d } }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match observation.rotation {
        RotationNotAttempted => BmcSecureRefused { cause: CredentialRotationNotApplied }
        AccountManagementUnavailable { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: d } }
        RotationApplied { reference: r, applied_at: at, evidence: e } =>
          adjudicate_rotation(
            observation: observation,
            reference: r,
            applied_at: at,
            rotation_evidence: e,
            environment: environment,
          )
      }
  }
}

fn derive_bmc_secure(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  policy: IntakeQualificationPolicy,
) -> BmcSecureStanding {
  let outcome = if same_intake_subject(left: subject, right: observation.subject) == false {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: subject, found: observation.subject } }
  } else {
    adjudicate_bootstrap(observation: observation, environment: policy.environment)
  }
  BmcSecureStanding { subject: subject, policy: policy, outcome: outcome }
}

data bmc_secure_phase: IntakePhase = Arrival { phase: BmcSecure }

fn bmc_secure_receipt_result(standing: BmcSecureStanding) -> IntakeReceiptResult {
  match standing.outcome {
    BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: _, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } => ReceiptSatisfied
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: c } =>
      ReceiptRefused { owner: bmc_secure_refusal_owner(cause: c), cause: bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c) }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_receipt_observations(standing: BmcSecureStanding) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  match standing.outcome {
    BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: e, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } => e
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: _ } => []
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_receipt(
  standing: BmcSecureStanding,
  producer: IntakeProducerIdentity,
  started_at: EpochMs,
  ended_at: EpochMs,
  previous_receipt: ContentHash?,
) -> IntakeReceiptEnvelope {
  IntakeReceiptEnvelope {
    schema: MachineIntakeReceiptV1,
    subject: standing.subject,
    phase: bmc_secure_phase,
    producer: producer,
    policy_digest: intake_qualification_policy_digest(policy: standing.policy),
    started_at: started_at,
    ended_at: ended_at,
    observations: bmc_secure_receipt_observations(standing: standing),
    result: bmc_secure_receipt_result(standing: standing),
    previous_receipt: previous_receipt,
  }
}

// ══ BmcSecure AS A DESIRED STATE (docs/plans/managed-host-untangle.md, cut O1b) ══════════════════
//
// THE DEFECT THIS SECTION REPAIRS. derive_bmc_secure above is rotation-EVENT shaped: a rejected
// bootstrap credential refuses PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired, an accepted one with no rotation
// refuses CredentialRotationNotApplied, and only RotationApplied with an advanced epoch can mint
// BmcSecured. So a correctly secured controller -- managed credential accepted, published credential
// refused on every LAN member of the channel census -- cannot be observed as already secured. The
// phase is decomposed here instead: observe the CURRENT account state (independent of whether this
// invocation rotated anything), Noop only when the existing conjunction already holds, otherwise
// Apply a typed account action over an admitted route, then re-read independently and derive the
// standing from that readback alone.
//
// THE CONJUNCTION AND THE CENSUS JOIN ARE NOT RESTATED. adjudicate_published_census above is the one
// authority for the published half; this section calls it with the observation's read floor where
// the event path passed applied_at, projecting observer instants to their millis only at that call.
// The managed half (accepted, read at or after the floor) is the same test adjudicate_managed_probe
// makes, over the observer clock.
//
// SHADOW, NOT YET THE AUTHORITY (operator ruling C, eager-gull-22, 2026-10-04). The event path above
// stays as the standing mtcollins1 and managed_hosts() read, FROZEN: no new consumer may use it. Its
// deletion and mtcollins1's re-expression in this shape are one held transition, made together with a
// committed read-only post-reflash probe and the operator-approved wet Apply on that unit
// (bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier). Until then the executing consumers of this section are its dry
// realization over gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld and that realization's witness.

// A CONTROLLER'S OWN CLOCK IS AN OBSERVATION OF THE CONTROLLER, NEVER AN ORDERING CLOCK. mtjade1's BMC
// reports the year 2000. The reading is kept, with its evidence, and it is not an ordering clock: every
// ordering field below is gunbc.clock_read ObserverClockInstant, which only the observer mints, and the
// sealed mints refuse this type at their call arguments. Not wider: a non-literal value of this type
// in a record field typed ObserverClockInstant is accepted today
// (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value).
type ControllerClockReading {
  reported_millis: EpochMs
  evidence: EvidenceRef
}

// ONE AUTHENTICATION ATTEMPT, TIMED BY THE OBSERVER. The three arms of CredentialProbeOutcome with an
// observer instant where it carries a bare EpochMs; the event path's type dies with the event path.
//
// EVERY ORDERING FIELD SITS IN A SEALED RECORD WHOSE MINT TAKES THE INSTANT AS A PARAMETER. A field
// typed ObserverClockInstant does not by itself keep another product out of it: a non-literal value
// of a distinct product placed in a record or variant field is accepted today
// (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value), while the same value at
// a call argument refuses. sole_constructor seals records, not coproduct arms, so the probe arms carry
// ObservedReading rather than an instant: a literal outside this module refuses SoleConstructorViolation,
// and the one mint, observed_reading, refuses a ControllerClockReading at its observed_at argument.
type ObservedReading sole_constructor {
  evidence: EvidenceRef
  observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

fn observed_reading(evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedReading {
  ObservedReading { evidence: evidence, observed_at: observed_at }
}

type ObservedCredentialProbe
  = ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: ObservedReading }
  | ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: ObservedReading }
  | ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

type ObservedPublishedLanProbe {
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber
  address: Ipv4Address
  probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
}

type PublishedAccountKind
  = PublishedAccountRetired
  | PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: PublishedCredentialRestorePath }
  | PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: RetainedCredentialKind }

type ObservedPublishedAccount sole_constructor {
  kind: PublishedAccountKind
  evidence: EvidenceRef
  observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

fn observed_published_account(kind: PublishedAccountKind, evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedPublishedAccount {
  ObservedPublishedAccount { kind: kind, evidence: evidence, observed_at: observed_at }
}

// THE CURRENT ACCOUNT STATE OF ONE CONTROLLER, AS READ. It carries no rotation and no bootstrap probe:
// it is the same reading whether or not anything was written. read_floor is the observer instant the
// read began; every reading in it must be at or after the floor, which is what lets the receipt below
// order a readback after the write it verifies and refuse the pre-write reading passed twice.
// firmware is the release the controller reported in the same read. It is the build a route must be
// grounded for: the plan reads it from here and takes no build argument, so a current reading cannot be
// admitted over a route for a build the controller no longer runs (O1a's stale-route crossing).
type BmcAccountStateObservation sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference
  read_floor: ObserverClockInstant
  managed_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef
  census_observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
  published_probes: List<ObservedPublishedLanProbe>
  published_user: IpmiUserId
  published_account: ObservedPublishedAccount
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference
  break_glass_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
  controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?
}

fn observed_bmc_account_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference,
  read_floor: ObserverClockInstant,
  managed_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe,
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: ObserverClockInstant,
  published_probes: List<ObservedPublishedLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: ObservedPublishedAccount,
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference,
  break_glass_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe,
  controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?,
) -> BmcAccountStateObservation {
  BmcAccountStateObservation {
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    firmware: firmware,
    managed: managed,
    read_floor: read_floor,
    managed_probe: managed_probe,
    channel_census: channel_census,
    census_evidence: census_evidence,
    census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
    published_probes: published_probes,
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: published_account,
    break_glass: break_glass,
    break_glass_probe: break_glass_probe,
    controller_clock: controller_clock,
  }
}

fn observed_probe_at_join(probe: ObservedCredentialProbe) -> CredentialProbeOutcome {
  match probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } => CredentialAccepted { evidence: r.evidence, observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at) }
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => CredentialRejected { evidence: r.evidence, observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at) }
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } => CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d }
  }
}

fn observed_published_account_at_join(account: ObservedPublishedAccount) -> PublishedCredentialAccountObservation {
  let at = observer_instant_millis(instant: account.observed_at)
  match account.kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: r } =>
      PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: r, evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: k } =>
      PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: k, evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
  }
}

fn managed_reference_same(a: ManagedCredentialReference, b: ManagedCredentialReference) -> Bool {
  a.account == b.account
    && a.role == b.role
    && (a.secret.project as String) == (b.secret.project as String)
    && a.secret.secret == b.secret.secret
    && a.secret.version == b.secret.version
    && a.credential_epoch == b.credential_epoch
}

// WHAT THE PHASE REQUIRES OF THE CONTROLLER: this managed generation accepted, the published
// credential closed, under this qualification policy.
// published_break_glass is the exact generation the published account is retired TO (or, under a
// break-glass retention policy, the account that must be the one retained): a predeclared secret,
// version and epoch. It is part of the goal so the replacement is a desired state and never whatever
// generation a caller hands the planner. Disabling or deleting the published account instead is not an
// arm here: those are channel and user-table writes no executed evidence grounds on any controller.
type BmcSecureGoal {
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference
  published_break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference
  policy: IntakeQualificationPolicy
}

// WHAT AN ASSESSMENT FOUND. The conjunction's own causes, plus the published account's replacement:
// the published user must authenticate with the goal's exact break-glass generation (break_glass /
// break_glass_probe on the reading), observed at or after the read floor. Without it, "factory rejected
// beside an arbitrary replacement" would read as secured, and an Apply could mint a receipt without the
// goal generation ever authenticating. Disable or delete of the published account is not an admitted
// goal arm here; it would carry its own observation, not ride on this probe.
type BmcSecureStateFinding
  = ConjunctionFinding { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | BreakGlassGenerationRejected
  | BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn bmc_secure_state_finding_label(finding: BmcSecureStateFinding) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match finding {
    ConjunctionFinding { cause: c } => bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c)
    BreakGlassGenerationRejected => "the published account does not authenticate with the goal's break-glass generation"
    BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the probe of the goal's break-glass generation did not establish a credential state"
  }
}

// The satisfied evidence: the conjunction's BmcSecured, kept with the observation it was read from.
type BmcSecureHeld {
  observation: BmcAccountStateObservation
  evidence: List<EvidenceRef>
}

type BmcSecureStateRefusal
  = AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: MachineIntakeSubject, found: MachineIntakeSubject }
  | AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: ManagedCredentialReference, observed: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: ObserverClockInstant }
  | AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause, operation: MissingAccountOperation }
  | AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: SecretRef, goal: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: ManagedCredentialReference, observed: ManagedCredentialReference }

// WHICH CONJUNCTION REFUSALS AN ACCOUNT WRITE CAN REMEDY, WHICH ARE UNKNOWNS, AND WHICH ARE NEITHER.
// A deviation is a state the account action changes (the managed credential not accepted, the
// published one still accepted or still holding channel access). An unknown is a reading that did not
// establish a state; it is never a deviation, because writing on an unread controller is the
// absorbing fallback DESIGN §5 forbids. Everything else -- an ordering, a duplicated or unmatched
// reading, a production retention -- refuses the assessment.
// THE ONLY ADMITTED ACTION IS A PASSWORD WRITE (IpmiSetUserPassword over a grounded route). It cannot
// give a LAN channel an address, set a channel's privilege to NO ACCESS, or put the factory password
// back, so a deviation only those operations change is not remediable here: it refuses with the
// missing operation named, rather than planning a password write that cannot clear it.
type MissingAccountOperation
  = ChannelAccessWrite
  | PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore

type ConjunctionCauseClass
  = CauseRemediableByAccountAction
  | CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: MissingAccountOperation }
  | CauseUnestablishedReading
  | CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
  | CauseRefusesAssessment

fn conjunction_cause_class(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> ConjunctionCauseClass {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => CauseRefusesAssessment
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => CauseRefusesAssessment
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    ManagedCredentialRejected => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: ChannelAccessWrite }
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: ChannelAccessWrite }
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedForProduction => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore }
  }
}

fn conjunction_over_observation(goal: BmcSecureGoal, observed: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  let floor = observer_instant_millis(instant: observed.read_floor)
  match observed.managed_probe {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialRejected }
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } }
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: mr } => {
      let me = mr.evidence
      let at = mr.observed_at
      if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: at, later: observed.read_floor) {
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: floor, probed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: at) } }
      } else {
        adjudicate_published_census(
          endpoint: observed.endpoint,
          reference: observed.managed,
          applied_at: floor,
          rotation_evidence: me,
          bootstrap: CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: "no bootstrap probe: the desired-state reading carries none" as NonEmptyStr },
          managed_evidence: me,
          census: observed.channel_census,
          census_evidence: observed.census_evidence,
          census_observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: observed.census_observed_at),
          probes: map(observed.published_probes, p => PublishedCredentialLanProbe { channel: p.channel, address: p.address, outcome: observed_probe_at_join(probe: p.probe) }),
          published_user: observed.published_user,
          published_account: observed_published_account_at_join(account: observed.published_account),
          environment: goal.policy.environment,
        )
      }
    }
  }
}

// Under a break-glass retention policy the retained account must be the goal's exact generation.
fn retention_is_goal_bound(kind: PublishedAccountKind, goal: BmcSecureGoal) -> Bool {
  match kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => true
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _ } => true
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: r } =>
      match r {
        PublishedFactoryCredential => true
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: sec } =>
          (sec.project as String) == (goal.published_break_glass.secret.project as String)
            && sec.secret == goal.published_break_glass.secret.secret
            && sec.version == goal.published_break_glass.secret.version
      }
  }
}

fn retained_secret_or_goal(kind: PublishedAccountKind, goal: BmcSecureGoal) -> SecretRef {
  match kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => goal.published_break_glass.secret
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _ } => goal.published_break_glass.secret
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: r } =>
      match r {
        PublishedFactoryCredential => goal.published_break_glass.secret
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: sec } => sec
      }
  }
}

fn assess_break_glass_generation(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
) -> GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if !managed_reference_same(a: goal.published_break_glass, b: observed.break_glass) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: goal.published_break_glass, observed: observed.break_glass } }
  } else {
    match observed.break_glass_probe {
      ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } =>
        GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: [], unknowns: FreeSemigroup { head: BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: d }, tail: [] } }
      ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } =>
        if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: r.observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) {
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
        } else {
          GoalDiverged { deviations: FreeSemigroup { head: BreakGlassGenerationRejected, tail: [] } }
        }
      ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } =>
        if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: r.observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) {
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
        } else {
          GoalSatisfied { evidence: BmcSecureHeld { observation: observed, evidence: concat(evidence, [r.evidence]) } }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn assess_bmc_account_state(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if !managed_reference_same(a: goal.managed, b: observed.managed) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: goal.managed, observed: observed.managed } }
  } else if !retention_is_goal_bound(kind: observed.published_account.kind, goal: goal) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: retained_secret_or_goal(kind: observed.published_account.kind, goal: goal), goal: goal.published_break_glass } }
  } else {
    match conjunction_over_observation(goal: goal, observed: observed) {
      BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: e, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } =>
        assess_break_glass_generation(goal: goal, observed: observed, evidence: e)
      BmcSecureRefused { cause: c } =>
        match conjunction_cause_class(cause: c) {
          CauseRemediableByAccountAction => GoalDiverged { deviations: FreeSemigroup { head: ConjunctionFinding { cause: c }, tail: [] } }
          CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: op } => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: c, operation: op } }
          CauseUnestablishedReading => GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: [], unknowns: FreeSemigroup { head: ConjunctionFinding { cause: c }, tail: [] } }
          CauseReadingPrecedesFloor => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
          CauseRefusesAssessment => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: c } }
        }
    }
  }
}

// The observer of this effect is the supplied reading: the read itself is the realization's (dry
// below; live is bmc_secure_state_live_read_frontier), and the observer refuses a reading of another
// subject rather than assessing it.
fn observe_bmc_account_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> ObservationAttempt<BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if same_intake_subject(left: subject, right: reading.subject) {
    ObservationEstablished { observed: reading }
  } else {
    ObservationRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: subject, found: reading.subject } }
  }
}

// What a divergence obliges: an account action, not yet admitted. Admission is the plan mint's.
type BmcAccountActionDue {
  deviation: BmcSecureStateFinding
}

fn decide_bmc_account_state(
  assessment: GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal>,
) -> UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> {
  match assessment {
    GoalSatisfied { evidence: _ } => Noop
    GoalDiverged { deviations: d } => Apply { plan: BmcAccountActionDue { deviation: d.head } }
    GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: u } => Refuse { reason: bmc_secure_state_finding_label(finding: u.head) }
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: c } => Refuse { reason: bmc_secure_state_refusal_label(cause: c) }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_state_refusal_label(cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match cause {
    AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: _, found: _ } => "the account-state reading belongs to another intake subject"
    AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: _, observed: _ } => "the account-state reading probed another managed credential generation than the goal names"
    AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: _ } => "an account-state reading precedes the observer instant its read began"
    AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: c } => bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c)
    AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: _, operation: op } =>
      match op {
        ChannelAccessWrite => "the deviation needs a channel-access write, and no admitted route performs one; a password write cannot clear it"
        PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore => "the policy retains the factory credential and it is not accepted; restoring it is not an admitted operation"
      }
    AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: _, goal: _ } => "the break-glass account retained by policy is not the generation the goal names"
    AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: _, observed: _ } => "the account-state reading probed another break-glass generation than the goal names"
  }
}

// THE EFFECT'S DOMAIN PROJECTION (gunbc.host_convergence_protocol): observe, assess, decide. Its row is
// gunbc.host_convergence_census BmcSecureAccountState. The protocol's apply side is an open frontier
// (host_effect_decide_apply_frontier, CONVERGENCE-ONE C8); the apply and the independent readback
// below are this domain's own, with its own sealed receipt, and do not discharge C8.
fn bmc_secure_state_projection() -> HostEffectDomainProjection<MachineIntakeSubject, BmcSecureGoal, BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal, BmcSecureStateRefusal, BmcAccountActionDue> {
  HostEffectDomainProjection {
    observe: observe_bmc_account_state,
    assess: assess_bmc_account_state,
    decide: decide_bmc_account_state,
  }
}

type BmcSecureStateInspection
  = BmcSecureStateInspected {
      observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
      assessment: GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal>,
      decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue>,
    }
  | BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }

fn inspect_bmc_secure_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecureStateInspection {
  let projection = bmc_secure_state_projection()
  match inspect_via_host_effect_projection(subject: subject, goal: goal, request: reading, projection: projection) {
    GoalObservationRefused { subject: _, goal: _, request: _, cause: c } => BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c }
    GoalInspected { subject: _, goal: _, request: _, observed: o, assessment: a } =>
      BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: projection.decide(a) }
  }
}

// ── THE SECRET ORDER, AS CARRIERS THE APPLY REQUIRES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The new credential generation is generated and STORED under the unit's SecretRef, and its EXACT
// resolved version is FETCHED, before any account write and before the managed probe. The earlier
// plan row that materialized the managed secret after BmcSecure was wrong: a rotation cannot first
// obtain its secret after it has completed. So the write's plan takes a Fetched generation, a Fetched
// generation can only be minted from a Stored one and a fetch that resolved to exactly the stored
// version, and every later consumer materializes that same generation through
// gunbc.auth.secret_ref_credential fetch_secret_ref_credential over the pinned reference the carrier
// holds. None of these carriers holds the secret bytes.

type ManagedCredentialGenerationStored sole_constructor {
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference
  stored_version: SmResolvedVersionIdentity
  stored_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type GenerationStoreRefusal
  = GenerationStoreForAnotherSecret { expected: NonEmptyStr, stored: SmResolvedVersionIdentity }
  | GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: String }

type GenerationStoreAdmission
  = GenerationStored { stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored }
  | GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreRefusal }

// current is the generation in force; the stored generation is the next epoch of the same account,
// role and secret, pinned to the exact version Secret Manager answered for the write (AddVersion's
// returned name), never an alias.
fn admit_stored_generation(
  current: ManagedCredentialReference,
  added: SmResolvedVersionIdentity,
  stored_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> GenerationStoreAdmission {
  match sm_resolved_version_secret_resource(identity: added) {
    SmVersionSecretNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } => GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } }
    SmVersionSecretProjected { secret_resource: sec } =>
      if !gcp_resource_names_this_secret(returned: sec as String, project: current.secret.project, project_number: fleet_secrets_project_number, secret: current.secret.secret) {
        GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreForAnotherSecret { expected: current.secret.secret, stored: added } }
      } else {
        match sm_resolved_version_id(identity: added) {
          SmVersionIdNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } => GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } }
          SmVersionIdProjected { version: v } =>
            GenerationStored {
              stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored {
                reference: ManagedCredentialReference {
                  account: current.account,
                  role: current.role,
                  secret: SecretRef { project: current.secret.project, secret: current.secret.secret, version: v, hash_state: HashPending },
                  credential_epoch: current.credential_epoch + 1,
                },
                stored_version: added,
                stored_at: stored_at,
              },
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

type ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched sole_constructor {
  stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored
  fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type GenerationFetchRefusal
  = GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | GenerationFetchResolvedAnotherVersion { stored: SmResolvedVersionIdentity, resolved: SmResolvedVersionIdentity }
  | GenerationFetchPrecedesStore { stored_at: ObserverClockInstant, fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant }

type GenerationFetchAdmission
  = GenerationFetched { fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched }
  | GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchRefusal }

fn admit_fetched_generation(
  stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored,
  fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> GenerationFetchAdmission {
  if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: fetched_at, later: stored.stored_at) {
    GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchPrecedesStore { stored_at: stored.stored_at, fetched_at: fetched_at } }
  } else {
    match fetch {
      SecretCredentialReady { credential: _, resolved_version: r } =>
        if (r as String) != (stored.stored_version as String) {
          GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchResolvedAnotherVersion { stored: stored.stored_version, resolved: r } }
        } else {
          GenerationFetched { fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched { stored: stored, fetched_at: fetched_at } }
        }
      SecretCredentialAccessUpsertRequired { plan: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access needs an access upsert first" as NonEmptyStr } }
      SecretCredentialWireDecodeRefused { identity_cause: _, payload_cause: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access response did not decode" as NonEmptyStr } }
      SecretCredentialFetchRefused { reason: why } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: why } }
      SecretCredentialResolvedVersionMismatch { requested: _, resolved: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access resolved another version than requested" as NonEmptyStr } }
    }
  }
}

// The pinned reference a later consumer passes to fetch_secret_ref_credential: the exact version, never
// the alias the generation was stored under.
fn fetched_generation_reference(fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched) -> ManagedCredentialReference {
  fetched.stored.reference
}

// ── THE ACCOUNT ACTION, ADMITTED OVER A GROUNDED ROUTE ───────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Two writes, each over its own admitted route: the managed account set to the fetched managed
// generation, and the published account retired by setting it to a fetched break-glass generation the
// fleet owns (the user-2 retirement mtcollins1 executed on 2026-09-13). Each admission is COMPUTED here
// by gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_rotation_route admit_rotation_apply from the route standing, the
// controller and build being written and the operator's approval; an admission is never received.
// Every arm other than RotationApplyAdmitted refuses before any write is planned, which is what
// is that module's rotation_route_consumption_frontier consumer in code; the frontier stands until this
// planner runs on a production path (the held cut-over).

type AccountWriteTarget
  = ManagedAccountTarget
  | PublishedAccountTarget

type PlannedAccountWrite {
  target: AccountWriteTarget
  user: IpmiUserId
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding
  request: BmcAccountWriteRequest
  decided_by: NonEmptyStr
  generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched
}

type BmcAccountActionPlan sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  goal: BmcSecureGoal
  diverged: BmcAccountStateObservation
  due: BmcAccountActionDue
  managed_write: PlannedAccountWrite
  published_write: PlannedAccountWrite
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type BmcAccountPlanRefusal
  = AccountPlanNotDue { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }
  | AccountPlanUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }
  | AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: AccountWriteTarget, admission: RotationApplyAdmission }
  | AccountWriteRequestNotIpmiUser { target: AccountWriteTarget, request: BmcAccountWriteRequest }
  | AccountWriteRequestForAnotherUser { target: AccountWriteTarget, admitted: IpmiUserId, required: IpmiUserId }
  | ManagedGenerationForAnotherAccount { generation: ManagedCredentialReference, in_force: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | ManagedGenerationNotAdvanced { in_force: Int, generation: Int }
  | PublishedGenerationNotGoalBound { generation: ManagedCredentialReference, goal: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | GenerationFetchedAfterPlan { target: AccountWriteTarget, fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant, planned_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | PlanPrecedesDivergedReading { read_floor: ObserverClockInstant, planned_at: ObserverClockInstant }

type BmcAccountPlanOutcome
  = BmcAccountPlanned { plan: BmcAccountActionPlan }
  | BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

fn admitted_account_write(
  target: AccountWriteTarget,
  user: IpmiUserId,
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  approval: Redemption,
  generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched,
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> PlannedAccountWriteAdmission {
  let admission = admit_rotation_apply(standing: route, target_endpoint: endpoint, target_firmware: firmware, approval: approval)
  match admission {
    RotationApplyAdmitted { standing: s, request: req, decided_by: by } =>
      match req {
        RedfishAccountPasswordWrite { transport_operation: _, action_shape: _ } =>
          PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteRequestNotIpmiUser { target: target, request: req } }
        IpmiSetUserPassword { user: u } =>
          if (u as Int) != (user as Int) {
            PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteRequestForAnotherUser { target: target, admitted: u, required: user } }
          } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: generation.fetched_at) {
            PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: GenerationFetchedAfterPlan { target: target, fetched_at: generation.fetched_at, planned_at: planned_at } }
          } else {
            PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted {
              write: PlannedAccountWrite { target: target, user: user, route: s, request: req, decided_by: by, generation: generation },
            }
          }
      }
    RotationApplyRouteNotGrounded { standing: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteForAnotherController { route_endpoint: _, target_endpoint: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteForAnotherBuild { route_firmware: _, target_firmware: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyApprovalRefused { cause: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyApprovalDenied => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyApprovalForAnotherAuthority { authority: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyApprovalForAnotherRequest { approved: _, requested: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
  }
}

type PlannedAccountWriteAdmission
  = PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: PlannedAccountWrite }
  | PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

// THE PLAN MINT RUNS THE DECISION ITSELF. A caller supplies the reading, the goal and the route
// inputs; it does not supply a decision, so an Apply cannot be planned over a Noop or a refusal.
fn plan_bmc_account_action(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  managed_route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  managed_approval: Redemption,
  managed_generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched,
  published_route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  published_approval: Redemption,
  published_generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched,
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> BmcAccountPlanOutcome {
  match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: subject, goal: goal, reading: reading) {
    BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanUnobserved { cause: c } }
    BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: _, decision: d } =>
      match d {
        Noop => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanNotDue { decision: d } }
        Refuse { reason: _ } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanNotDue { decision: d } }
        Apply { plan: due } =>
          if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: o.read_floor) {
            BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: PlanPrecedesDivergedReading { read_floor: o.read_floor, planned_at: planned_at } }
          } else {
            let next = fetched_generation_reference(fetched: managed_generation)
            let in_force = goal.managed
            if !(next.account == in_force.account && next.role == in_force.role && (next.secret.project as String) == (in_force.secret.project as String) && next.secret.secret == in_force.secret.secret) {
              BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: ManagedGenerationForAnotherAccount { generation: next, in_force: in_force } }
            } else if next.credential_epoch <= in_force.credential_epoch {
              BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: ManagedGenerationNotAdvanced { in_force: in_force.credential_epoch, generation: next.credential_epoch } }
            } else if !managed_reference_same(a: fetched_generation_reference(fetched: published_generation), b: goal.published_break_glass) {
              BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: PublishedGenerationNotGoalBound { generation: fetched_generation_reference(fetched: published_generation), goal: goal.published_break_glass } }
            } else {
              match admitted_account_write(target: ManagedAccountTarget, user: managed_user, route: managed_route, endpoint: o.endpoint, firmware: o.firmware, approval: managed_approval, generation: managed_generation, planned_at: planned_at) {
                PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: c }
                PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: mw } =>
                  match admitted_account_write(target: PublishedAccountTarget, user: o.published_user, route: published_route, endpoint: o.endpoint, firmware: o.firmware, approval: published_approval, generation: published_generation, planned_at: planned_at) {
                    PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: c }
                    PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: pw } =>
                      BmcAccountPlanned {
                        plan: BmcAccountActionPlan {
                          subject: subject,
                          endpoint: o.endpoint,
                          firmware: o.firmware,
                          goal: BmcSecureGoal { managed: next, published_break_glass: goal.published_break_glass, policy: goal.policy },
                          diverged: o,
                          due: due,
                          managed_write: mw,
                          published_write: pw,
                          planned_at: planned_at,
                        },
                      }
                  }
              }
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

// ── THE APPLICATION RECEIPT AND THE PHASE RECEIPT ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// What the effect did, as the realization recorded it: each write's completion, the request and
// response receipts, and the observer instant the application completed. Minted only by a realization
// of the plan in this module (the dry one below; the live one is bmc_secure_state_live_apply_frontier).
type BmcAccountApplication sole_constructor {
  plan: BmcAccountActionPlan
  managed_write_completed: Bool
  published_write_completed: Bool
  request_receipt: EvidenceRef
  response_receipt: EvidenceRef
  applied_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type BmcSecurePhaseDecision
  = BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: BmcAccountStateObservation }
  | BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: BmcAccountActionPlan, application: BmcAccountApplication, post_read: BmcAccountStateObservation }

// THE PHASE'S DOMAIN RECEIPT. gunbc.ensure says of itself that its observations and satisfaction
// Booleans are caller-supplied and that one observation can be passed twice, so the ensure shape is the
// decision only. This carrier binds subject + phase + admitted plan + application receipt +
// independent post-read + evidence, and it is sealed: its two mints below are the only constructors,
// one for a reading that already held (Noop) and one for an application followed by a readback. The
// readback is independent BY ORDERING, not by convention: its read floor must be at or after the
// application's observer instant, which is after the plan, which is after the diverged reading, so the
// pre-write reading cannot be passed as the post-read.
type BmcSecurePhaseReceipt sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  phase: IntakePhase
  goal: BmcSecureGoal
  decision: BmcSecurePhaseDecision
  held: BmcSecureHeld
}

type BmcSecurePhaseRefusal
  = PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }
  | PhaseNotHeld { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }
  | ApplicationIncomplete { managed_write_completed: Bool, published_write_completed: Bool, response_receipt: EvidenceRef }
  | PostReadForAnotherController { expected: BmcControllerEndpoint, found: BmcControllerEndpoint }
  | PostReadPrecedesApplication { applied_at: ObserverClockInstant, read_floor: ObserverClockInstant }
  | ApplicationPrecedesPlan { planned_at: ObserverClockInstant, applied_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | PostReadNotHeld { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }

type BmcSecurePhaseOutcome
  = BmcSecurePhaseConverged { receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt }
  | BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: BmcSecurePhaseRefusal }

fn bmc_secure_phase_noop(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecurePhaseOutcome {
  match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: subject, goal: goal, reading: reading) {
    BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: c } }
    BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: d } =>
      match a {
        GoalSatisfied { evidence: held } =>
          BmcSecurePhaseConverged {
            receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt { subject: subject, phase: bmc_secure_phase, goal: goal, decision: BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: o }, held: held },
          }
        GoalDiverged { deviations: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
        GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
        GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
      }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_applied(
  application: BmcAccountApplication,
  post_read: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecurePhaseOutcome {
  let plan = application.plan
  if !(application.managed_write_completed && application.published_write_completed) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused {
      cause: ApplicationIncomplete {
        managed_write_completed: application.managed_write_completed,
        published_write_completed: application.published_write_completed,
        response_receipt: application.response_receipt,
      },
    }
  } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: application.applied_at, later: plan.planned_at) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: ApplicationPrecedesPlan { planned_at: plan.planned_at, applied_at: application.applied_at } }
  } else if (post_read.endpoint.host as String) != (plan.endpoint.host as String) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadForAnotherController { expected: plan.endpoint, found: post_read.endpoint } }
  } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: post_read.read_floor, later: application.applied_at) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadPrecedesApplication { applied_at: application.applied_at, read_floor: post_read.read_floor } }
  } else {
    match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: plan.subject, goal: plan.goal, reading: post_read) {
      BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: c } }
      BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: d } =>
        match a {
          GoalSatisfied { evidence: held } =>
            BmcSecurePhaseConverged {
              receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt {
                subject: plan.subject,
                phase: bmc_secure_phase,
                goal: plan.goal,
                decision: BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: plan, application: application, post_read: o },
                held: held,
              },
            }
          GoalDiverged { deviations: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
          GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_receipt_evidence(receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  match receipt.decision {
    BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: _ } => receipt.held.evidence
    BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: _, application: a, post_read: _ } =>
      concat([a.request_receipt, a.response_receipt], receipt.held.evidence)
  }
}

// ── THE DRY REALIZATION OVER gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld ────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The executing consumer of this section while it is in shadow. The world's IPMI user table is the
// controller; the realization writes it through bmc_ipmi_set_user_password and reads it through
// bmc_ipmi_user_accepts, so the readback is a property of the world after the write and never the
// write's own completion. The channel census and the published user's channel access are inputs of
// the read (BmcWorld does not model channels); the probes against every addressable LAN member are
// derived from the world. The secret bytes each write uses are materialized through a
// SecretCredentialFetch that must resolve to exactly the generation the plan carries.

data bmc_secure_dry_realization_name: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure dry realization over gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld" as NonEmptyStr

fn dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: EpochMs) -> ObserverClockInstant {
  observer_clock_modeled(millis: millis, realization: bmc_secure_dry_realization_name)
}

fn dry_evidence(text: String) -> EvidenceRef {
  EvidenceRef { label: text as NonEmptyStr, digest: content_hash_of_value(value: text) }
}

fn dry_probe(world: BmcWorld, user: IpmiUserId, password: String, what: String, at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedCredentialProbe {
  let text = join(["dry ipmi probe ", what, " user ", to_string(user as Int), " at ", to_string(observer_instant_millis(instant: at) as Int)], "")
  if bmc_ipmi_user_accepts(world: world, user: user, password: password) {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: observed_reading(evidence: dry_evidence(text: concat(text, " -> accepted")), observed_at: at) }
  } else {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: observed_reading(evidence: dry_evidence(text: concat(text, " -> rejected")), observed_at: at) }
  }
}

fn dry_published_lan_probes(
  world: BmcWorld,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_password: String,
  at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> List<ObservedPublishedLanProbe> {
  fold(census.members, init: [], f: (acc, m) =>
    match m {
      IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: _, medium: _ } => acc
      IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
        match cfg {
          IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned => acc
          IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } =>
            concat(acc, [ObservedPublishedLanProbe { channel: ch, address: a, probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: published_user, password: published_password, what: "published", at: at) }])
        }
    })
}

// ONE READ OF THE WORLD'S ACCOUNT STATE. read_at_millis is the realization's observer schedule; every
// reading in the observation is taken at it.
fn dry_read_bmc_account_state(
  world: BmcWorld,
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  managed_password: String,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_password: String,
  published_account: PublishedAccountKind,
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference,
  break_glass_password: String,
  read_at_millis: EpochMs,
) -> BmcAccountStateObservation {
  let at = dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: read_at_millis)
  observed_bmc_account_state(
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    firmware: firmware,
    managed: managed,
    read_floor: at,
    managed_probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: managed_user, password: managed_password, what: "managed", at: at),
    channel_census: census,
    census_evidence: dry_evidence(text: join(["dry channel census of ", endpoint.host as String, " at ", to_string(read_at_millis as Int)], "")),
    census_observed_at: at,
    published_probes: dry_published_lan_probes(world: world, census: census, published_user: published_user, published_password: published_password, at: at),
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: observed_published_account(
      kind: published_account,
      evidence: dry_evidence(text: join(["dry user list of ", endpoint.host as String, " at ", to_string(read_at_millis as Int)], "")),
      observed_at: at,
    ),
    break_glass: break_glass,
    break_glass_probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: published_user, password: break_glass_password, what: "break-glass", at: at),
    controller_clock: none,
  )
}

type BmcAccountDryStep {
  world: BmcWorld
  application: BmcAccountApplication
}

fn dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: SecretCredentialFetch, write: PlannedAccountWrite) -> String? {
  match fetch {
    SecretCredentialReady { credential: c, resolved_version: r } =>
      if (r as String) == (write.generation.stored.stored_version as String) { Present { value: c as String } } else { none }
    SecretCredentialAccessUpsertRequired { plan: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialWireDecodeRefused { identity_cause: _, payload_cause: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialFetchRefused { reason: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialResolvedVersionMismatch { requested: _, resolved: _ } => none
  }
}

// THE WRITES, IN THE SECRET ORDER. Each write's bytes come from a fetch that resolved to exactly that
// write's generation; a fetch of any other version writes nothing, and the application records the
// write as not completed rather than writing a different credential.
fn dry_apply_bmc_account_plan(
  world: BmcWorld,
  plan: BmcAccountActionPlan,
  managed_fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  published_fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  applied_at_millis: EpochMs,
) -> BmcAccountDryStep {
  let managed_step = match dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: managed_fetch, write: plan.managed_write) {
    Absent => BmcIpmiSetUserPasswordStep { world: world, completed: false }
    Present { value: pw } => bmc_ipmi_set_user_password(world: world, user: plan.managed_write.user, password: pw)
  }
  let published_step = match dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: published_fetch, write: plan.published_write) {
    Absent => BmcIpmiSetUserPasswordStep { world: managed_step.world, completed: false }
    Present { value: pw } => bmc_ipmi_set_user_password(world: managed_step.world, user: plan.published_write.user, password: pw)
  }
  let request_text = join(
    ["dry ", account_write_request_text(request: plan.managed_write.request) as String, " then ", account_write_request_text(request: plan.published_write.request) as String, " on ", plan.endpoint.host as String],
    "",
  )
  let response_text = join(
    [request_text, " -> managed completed=", if managed_step.completed { "true" } else { "false" }, " published completed=", if published_step.completed { "true" } else { "false" }],
    "",
  )
  BmcAccountDryStep {
    world: published_step.world,
    application: BmcAccountApplication {
      plan: plan,
      managed_write_completed: managed_step.completed,
      published_write_completed: published_step.completed,
      request_receipt: dry_evidence(text: request_text),
      response_receipt: dry_evidence(text: response_text),
      applied_at: dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: applied_at_millis),
    },
  }
}

// ── DECLARED FRONTIERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

data bmc_secure_state_live_read_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when a live read of a controller's account state mints BmcAccountStateObservation beside dry_read_bmc_account_state from IPMI user-test and channel-census transport calls, including the user test of the published account with the goal's exact break-glass generation (break_glass_probe) materialized through fetch_secret_ref_credential, timed by gunbc.clock_read observer_clock_read, with every probe and census response committed as content-addressed evidence; NOT satisfied by the dry realization, by a transcription of an older readback, or by a read whose instants come from the controller's clock" as NonEmptyStr,
)

data bmc_secure_state_live_apply_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when a live realization of BmcAccountActionPlan mints BmcAccountApplication beside dry_apply_bmc_account_plan, materializing each write's bytes through gunbc.auth.secret_ref_credential fetch_secret_ref_credential over that write's pinned generation reference, under the controller's own operator go-ahead redeemed through gunbc.auth.approval_broker; NOT satisfied by the dry realization, by a workflow entry that has not executed, or by a write whose bytes were supplied out of band" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// THE HELD TRANSITION (operator ruling C, 2026-10-04). Its rung drop is
// gunbc.rung_drop.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing_predates_reflash, retired by the same trigger.
data bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when mtcollins1's BmcSecure standing is derived by the state-shaped fold (bmc_secure_phase_noop or bmc_secure_phase_applied) from a committed post-reflash readback of the current subject, and the rotation-event path (derive_bmc_secure, BmcCredentialRotationObservation, CredentialRotationApplication, CredentialProbeOutcome and every consumer that reads them, including gunbc.managed_host managed_hosts and gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge BmcCredentialReestablishment) is deleted in the same change; NOT satisfied by this section typechecking, by its dry realization, by re-expressing the 2026-09-13 readback on BMC 0.32, or by a readback whose subject is not the unit's current firmware" as NonEmptyStr,
)
